{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T17:08:11.670Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"897c90c1b80c3e3bf21a36a6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:08:11.670Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"R7 capability check also inspected the public SDK 2026.10.27 declarations from a credential-free npm pack without changing the pin. No native expected item/hash/history-head precondition was exported there either. RelationshipEventStore.expectedVersion guards its separate relationship ledger, not native item parent/dependency/lifecycle writes. Additional SDK facade audit: index.ts importRelations forward updates and compensation also call an opaque PmClient.update without a history precondition; that facade cannot enforce a native item CAS with its current client contract. These sites join sync commitLocal and resolution publication under upstream #1576. The fixed-clock probe fails all 18 cases: history advances in all 18; 15 return incorrect success; 6 overwrite the peer title; all 18 change item state after the peer edit. Revert proof is not applicable to an unimplemented SDK contract; the finding remains unresolved, not marked fixed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T17:08:11.670Z"}],"before_hash":"8b005bd90f4307197a295bf1f7a5c814d422906a55864a49c8b81a60bebb99bd","after_hash":"eccf18bba225a257c846e68c4f443732764095c4aa203ab9dc3f6868cc241c25","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"579ec96708e63d1e574290ab918d728683a62b2b10061c763ad47d3cb8b23a6a"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T20:28:55.118Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"897c90c1b80c3e3bf21a36a6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:28:55.116Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"R8 implements the owner-approved package fallback for upstream pm-cli#1576: native history length/hash before inspection; SDK lifecycle write inside a workspace transaction; locked post-write native author/op/patch verification; selective append-only compensation and typed conflict if another entry intervened. Journal keys bind the head, and unverified dispatch/verified-but-uncommitted journals resume without redispatch. The missing native pre-write API remains an upstream follow-up, rather than an unmet package acceptance criterion. Existing SDK hooks and runtime remain active; native clients and sync adapters share history-fence.ts."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T20:28:55.118Z"}],"before_hash":"eccf18bba225a257c846e68c4f443732764095c4aa203ab9dc3f6868cc241c25","after_hash":"897d43a2b7a6b32492031d4e11857853e6a32b063eeb08935094987580e9bf27","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"6fbc2733ad66946c5f44505003e1eddd5fe5f0276857503f1815680cb2817ed5"}
